Z||000008||Taijiguy||06-29-2000||08:43 AM||||Hit and run is a cowards way out. My street is commony referred to (by me) as Hit and Run Hill. I've been victomized personally twice, then my mom's brand new Saturn got crunched by some kid whom I caught, and turned out didn't have insurance. We took mercy on him and agreed to let him pay my moms deductible of 500 in installements, of which he made maybe 3 (150 total) then dissapeared. My neigbor had her Toyota Camery smashed to bits by some drunk idiot in a pickup. After knocking her car 20 feet (this is a 25 mph residential area!) he and his buddies tried to take off. Only her large, loud, and highly aggresive boyfriend kept him from running. Well, him and a busted tie rod on the truck. Some people have no honor, decency, or honesty. Sad state of affairs. <BR>Sorry about your ride dude. Hope it all works out.<P>Taiji||||reg||1
